                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eb898819-9014-3061-83ee-d479dd2a7906",
                        "entry_id": "7604dce9-82f2-3422-921d-9aca4e6f5bab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "хим. соль хлороводородной (соляной) кислоты HCl"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "250c96e9-4eb0-4c15-807c-da3bf253026b",
                                "sense_id": "eb898819-9014-3061-83ee-d479dd2a7906",
                                "text": "Хлорид цезия, содержащий катионы сильного основания и анионы сильной кислоты, дает в растворе реакцию, близкую к нейтральной."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "93d5d1c3-6870-3402-a5fc-69bf4e85e40b",
                        "entry_id": "7604dce9-82f2-3422-921d-9aca4e6f5bab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "хим. анион хлороводородной (соляной) кислоты Cl⁻"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "95fc677b-d3f8-42d0-99c0-3a12579a0bbe",
                                "sense_id": "93d5d1c3-6870-3402-a5fc-69bf4e85e40b",
                                "text": "Концентрации хлорид- и сульфат-ионов и ионов меди не вызывают опасений, так как не выходят за пределы ПДК."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "61e573f5-3cc8-31b7-bc36-44f64541fc80",
                        "entry_id": "7604dce9-82f2-3422-921d-9aca4e6f5bab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "хим. хлорсодержащее соединение, содержащее ковалентную связь хлор-элемент"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "713973af-b6cf-4ccb-b900-d603f6511c61",
                                "sense_id": "61e573f5-3cc8-31b7-bc36-44f64541fc80",
                                "text": "Полученные из 2,5-дихлордигидропиразина (этот хлорид является производным энола дикетопиперазина) амидины со временем претерпевают десмотропную перегруппировку"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f84d5f9e-08e7-4a40-8375-90d65f9ba064",
                        "source_entry_id": "7604dce9-82f2-3422-921d-9aca4e6f5bab",
                        "target_lang_word": "chloride",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chloride",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "47517bbd-f0c4-3b34-81eb-a16b656e0bbb",
                                        "entry_id": "a6ff7b9e-c48a-3329-9cee-c67671dca549",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any binary compound of chlorine and another element or radical."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8b3b8684-b45d-3e29-a1c9-d9965877b89e",
                                        "entry_id": "a6ff7b9e-c48a-3329-9cee-c67671dca549",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any binary compound of chlorine and another element or radical.",
                                            "Any salt of hydrochloric acid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc7cee50-4007-421a-bbd6-fcf2e15b46eb",
                                                "sense_id": "8b3b8684-b45d-3e29-a1c9-d9965877b89e",
                                                "text": "Another type, also common in the Taipei area has more chlorides than sulfates, and while it is also hot, its flavor is more salty than sour. The springs at Chinshan on the north coast are typical of this type."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48d131fb-8dc8-4f83-a8c5-95a2ca0f135b",
                                                "sense_id": "8b3b8684-b45d-3e29-a1c9-d9965877b89e",
                                                "text": "Klopfer and Gamble (1966) gave 16 female goats (C. hircus) 5 min of contact with their young at parturition. Nine of the mothers had been temporarily rendered anosmic (could not smell) at parturition by spraying a 10% cocaine hydrogen chloride solution into their nostrils 20–90 min prior to parturition. […] Eight of the nine females who were anosmic at parturition but could smell at reintroduction accepted their own offspring, as well as alien young during reinstatement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4013ed23-c435-4a28-b24d-91afbf88a6a7",
                                                "sense_id": "8b3b8684-b45d-3e29-a1c9-d9965877b89e",
                                                "text": "The Renew is also free of polyvinyl chloride, asbestos, chlorofluorocarbons and halons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f16c534b-0030-42c0-90b0-6abf65500760",
                                                "sense_id": "8b3b8684-b45d-3e29-a1c9-d9965877b89e",
                                                "text": "McCoy’s team, including 66 researchers across four continents, found the salt and minerals left behind as water on Bennu, or its larger parent asteroid, evaporated. The minerals include sodium phosphates, carbonates, sulfates, chlorides and fluorides, some of which are necessary to the formation of life."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "67deaa11-aaad-30c2-b8d4-4e428c5a217e",
                                        "entry_id": "a6ff7b9e-c48a-3329-9cee-c67671dca549",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The anionic form of a chlorine atom."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f4df527b-ffc5-4b59-8d5f-67f07e8e6e6c",
